<title>USA: KeyCorp in pact to sell seven branches.</title>
<headline>KeyCorp in pact to sell seven branches.</headline>
<dateline>CLEVELAND 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>KeyCorp said Monday it reached a definitive agreement to sell seven of its branches to FirstFederal Financial Services Corp.</p>
<p>Terms of the sale were not disclosed.</p>
<p>KeyCorp said the branches have total deposits of about $160 million and loans of $24 million and employ about fifty people.</p>
<p>The company said First Federal has agreed to offer employment to all employees of the branches.</p>
<p>KeyCorp said it expects to complete the sale during the third quarter of 1997.</p>
<p>((-- New York newsdesk, 212-859-1610))</p>
